Converting List to List

I have a list of integers, `List` and I'd like to convert all the integer objects into Strings, thus finishing up with a new `List`.

Naturally, I could create a new `List` and loop through the list calling `String.valueOf()` for each integer, but I was wondering if there was a better (read: more automatic) way of doing it?

Just for fun, a solution using the jsr166y fork-join framework that should in JDK7.


    import java.util.concurrent.forkjoin.*;
    private final ForkJoinExecutor executor = new ForkJoinPool();
    ...
    List ints = ...;
    List strs =
    ParallelArray.create(ints.size(), Integer.class, executor)
    .withMapping(new Ops.Op() { public String op(Integer i) {
    return String.valueOf(i);
    }})
    .all()
    .asList();


(Disclaimer: Not compiled. Spec is not finalised. Etc.)

Unlikely to be in JDK7 is a bit of type inference and syntactical sugar to make that withMapping call less verbose:


     .withMapping(#(Integer i) String.valueOf(i))

