Retrieve the later date from a collection in Java 

I was retrieving some date records from my database with the following results:


    Date
    09/18/2012 1:34:34 AM
    09/8/2012 8:15:34 AM
    09/8/2012 12:02:11 AM
    08/30/2012 8:47:02 PM
    08/29/2012 11:44:00 PM


As from the list above, there are 2 dates with 09/8/2012 that I would like to select 09/8/2012 8:15:34 AM (the later one), thus my result will look like this:


    Date
    09/18/2012 1:34:34 AM
    09/8/2012 8:15:34 AM
    08/30/2012 8:47:02 PM
    08/29/2012 11:44:00 PM


How can I go about doing this? Thanks in advance :)

You could use SortedSet to arrange all your Dates from low to high.  
You could use either iterator() or descendingIterator() methods of TreeSet.  
Here is an example 


     TreeSet set = new TreeSet();
    DateFormat df = new SimpleDateFormat("dd.MM.yyyy HH:mm");
    set.add(df.parse("01.01.2000 12:00"));
    set.add(df.parse("01.01.2000 09:00"));
    set.add(df.parse("01.01.2000 18:00"));
    System.out.println("First date: " + set.first());
    System.out.println("Last date: " + set.last());
    System.out.println("From low to high:");
    for (Date date : set)
    System.out.println(date);
    System.out.println("From high to low:");
    Iterator backIterator = set.descendingIterator();
    while (backIterator.hasNext())
    System.out.println(backIterator.next());

