You cannot return separate structures via one method call, but you can return a composite of them. For example, returning a list of your lists would be a possible solution:


     public List> returnTwoArrayList()
    {
    List startDates = new ArrayList();
    List endDates = new ArrayList();
    List> result = new ArrayList>();
    result.add(startDates);
    result.add(endDates);
    return result;
    }


You can use `get()` method to retrieve these lists later on. Suppose you have made a call like `List> twoLists = returnTwoArrayList();` then you can get `startDate` by calling `twoLists.get(0)` and similarly `endDate` with `twoLists.get(1)`

