List iteration type mismatch 


    List holder = new List();
    holder.add(new JTabbedPane());
    holder.add(new JTabbedPane());
    for(JTabbedPane tab : holder)
    {
    System.out.println(tab.toString());
    }


Why it is showing error on type mismatch in for-each loop?


    Try:
    for(Object tab : holder)
    {
    System.out.println( ( (JTabbedPane )tab).toString());
    }


It is showing error because holder `is List of Object , not List of JTabbedPane`. So when you use for-each loop with `for(JTabbedPane tab : holder)` , It will show compilation error.

How can I sort a map contains another map by numbers 

I have a HashMap of type:


    HashMap>


This HashMap has values like


    {name, {dateasString, numberOfTasks}} 


I want to sort this by `numberOfTasks`. I can't find the way to do that.

You can't sort a `HashMap`, but you can get a sorted Array (or a List) of the keys. How you want to define your sort is up to you - just modify the comparator (or the `numberOfTasks` function that it calls:)

So something like this?


    public static void main() {
    final
    HashMap> map = new HashMap>();
    String[] keys = (String[]) map.keySet().toArray();
    Arrays.sort(keys, new Comparator() {
    @Override
    public int compare(String k1, String k2) {
    int v1 = numberOfTasks(map.get(k1));
    int v2 = numberOfTasks(map.get(k2));
    return Integer.valueOf(v1).compareTo(Integer.valueOf(v2));
    }
    });
    // 'keys' is now sorted the way you want.
    }
    public static int numberOfTasks(HashMap map) {
    int max = 0;
    for (Integer i : map.values()) {
    if (i > max) max = i;
    }
    return max;
    }

