My question:

How can I find the highest game score in the map collection?

Use a sorted collection like `TreeMap` which keeps its entries (key-value mappings) in natural order of their keys. Since, you want to sort on the high scores keep your scores as the keys and players as their values.

It's very likely that two or more players could have the same high scores. So, instead of mapping a score to a player we would have to map it to a `List` of players (with the same high score):


    // {key - value} = {high score - {list, of, players}}
    TreeMap> highestScores =
    new TreeMap>();
    for (Client client : getPlayers()) {
    List playerList = null;
    // make gameScore private
    Integer score = client.getGameScore(); // using getters() recommended
    // check if a player with this score already exists
    if ((playerList = highestScores.get(score)) == null) { // if NOT,
    playerList = new ArrayList(1); // CREATE a new list
    playerList.add(client);
    highestScores.put(score, playerList);
    } else { // if YES, ADD to the existing list
    playerList.add(client);
    }
    }


To iterate over all the high scores use


    for (Integer score : highestScores.descendingKeySet()) {
    for (Client player : highestScores.get(score)) { // iterate over player list
    System.out.println(player.getName() + ": " + score); // assuming "name" property
    }
    }


