If your `itemId` should be unique (recommended). You should use `Map` where `Integer` will have the unique Id of your `Item`, in this way you can use `get(itemId)` and `remove(itemId)` on map easily and you won't need any loops as well.  Otherwise(not recommended), you have to iterate over your list and find the first (or all) matching `itemId` from the list and than only you can remove that item. You can not remove the item directly from `List` by `list.remove(itemId)`. One another way is to maintain two list one for itemIds and one for Item. Whenever you add element to Item list add id of item to second list.  FOR EXAMPLE


    List itemList = new ArrayList();
    List itemIdList = new ArrayList();
    int itemIdWantToRemove = itemIdList.indexOf(itemId);
    itemList.remove(itemIdWantToRemove);
    itemIdList.remove(itemIdWantToRemove);

