Given your current implementation, you would need to loop over the list and find the `Item`(s) which have a matching `id` Something like...


    int deleteId = s.nextInt();
    Iterator it = items.iterator();
    while (it.hasNext()) {
    Item next = it.next();
    if (next.getId() == deleteId) {
    it.remove();
    }
    }


Equally you could also take advantage of Java 8's stream support and do something like...


    int deleteId = s.nextInt();
    List results = items.stream().filter((Item t) -> { return t.getId() == deleteId; }).collect(Collectors.toList());


You could then use the resulting `List` to remove all the elements in it from the `items` list...


    items.removeAll(results);


*Another possibility Is to find the first `Item` which matches the required id...


    int deleteId = s.nextInt();
    Item item = list.stream().filter(x -> 
    {
    return x.getId() == deleteId;
    })
    .findFirst()
    .get();
    if (item != null) {
    items.remove(item);
    }

