However, the list is not sorted. 1) Instead implementing `Comparator`, implement `Comparable` 2) You don't need to pass a `Comparator` to the call to `Collections.sort`, just pass the list:


    Collections.sort(list);


3) You should check for nulls properly in your `compareTo()` method to prevent these type of errors. If a1.value or a2.values is null, a `NullPointerException` will be thrown. It would be better to check for null in advance.

