Getting oldest DateTime in a List? I have a list of Dog `Entities` that contain the field `"Birthday".` I would like to have a method in the entity class that returns only the oldest `DateTime` in the list.  How can I do so? Entity:


    @Entity
    @Table(name = "DOG")
    public class Dog
    {
    //some other fields
    @Column(name = "BIRTHDAY")
    @Type(type = "org.jadira.usertype.dateandtime.joda.PersistentDateTime")
    private DateTime birthday;


Example of List:


    private List dogList;


Here is an example without lambada expressions:


    public DateTime findOldestDogsBirthday() {
    Collections.sort(dogList, new Comparator() {
    @Override
    public int compare(Dog o1, Dog o2) {
    DateTime d1 = o1.getBirthday();
    DateTime d2 = o2.getBirthday();
    return d1.compareTo(d2);
    }
    });
    return !dogList.isEmpty() ? dogList.get(0).getBirthday() : null;
    }

