SO community can you please give me some hints on my problem.  I don't really see the need for your own `OrderList`. Since `Order` is an abstract class, you can only add instances of non-abstract child classes to any `List` that you declare. Also, instead of


    class OrderList {
    private ArrayList list;
    public OrderList() {
    list = new ArrayList();
    }
    }


you can also use


    class OrderList extends ArrayList {
    public OrderList() {
    super();
    }
    }


and then simply use the `add(Order element)` that you inherited from your parent class. But then again, it might be more convenient to just declare an `ArrayList` wherever you intended to use your `OrderList`, as long as you don't add any new methods (that are not given by a regular `List`) to justify having an extra class.

