difference between TreeSets based on their interface Is there any difference between the two TreeSets ?:


    Set s = new TreeSet();
    SortedSet s = new TreeSet();


Calling `new HashSet()` will always create an empty `HashSet`. While these are all different instances, they are equal, regardless of whether you assign them to a `HashSet`, a `Set` or even a plain old `Object`. Note, however, that `HashSet` is not a `SortedSet`, and the second statement in the question will cause a compilation error.

