Looping over a huge list, check string equal to true I have a requirement as below:


    List userList = listOfUsers(); // Morethan 50,000 users


I need to find a user status from the list of users. if any one of the users is active then break the loop. what is the efficient way to handle this in java ? I would certainly think about using Java 8 Lambda. I have written an example class:


    package com.chocksaway;
    import java.util.ArrayList;
    import java.util.List;
    /**
    * Author milesd on 05/06/2017.
    */
    class Name {
    private String name;
    private Boolean status;
    public Name(String name, Boolean status) {
    this.name = name;
    this.status = status;
    }
    public String getName() {
    return name;
    }
    public Boolean getStatus() {
    return status;
    }
    }
    public class FindFirstInStream {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
    List userList = new ArrayList<>();
    userList.add(new Name("James", false));
    userList.add(new Name("Eric", true));
    userList.add(new Name("David", false));
    Name firstActiveName = userList.stream()
    .filter(e -> e.getStatus().equals(true))
    .findFirst()
    .get();
    System.out.println(firstActiveName.getName());
    }
    }


* * *

I've created a Name class, with name, and status. I populate a userList with James, Eric, and David. I use Java 8 stream to filter, and return the first "active" name (Eric). This is stored in "firstActiveName".

